                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c615531c-8488-4768-8c39-dbe8a5b2603d",
                        "source_entry_id": "9222bbfa-f6bc-3244-a253-0029e0eba6e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "0c66d921-2c89-35b0-b4bc-e8efbcdf9382",
                        "source_sense_description": "Christentum: eine Predigt in enger Anlehnung an einen Bibeltext, eine erbauliche Predigt",
                        "target_lang_word": "homily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "homily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c135975-e047-335f-885d-c3c12b7f5259",
                                        "entry_id": "1e35f580-cd44-39f8-8ad7-971fa504ac73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sermon, especially concerning a practical matter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1603679-c008-404f-9429-9185220ce959",
                                                "sense_id": "3c135975-e047-335f-885d-c3c12b7f5259",
                                                "text": "O moſt gentle Iupiter! What tedious homilie of Loue haue you wearied your pariſhioners withall, and neuer cri'de, haue patience good people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3621303b-82bd-4638-83d3-95e7a67a228c",
                                                "sense_id": "3c135975-e047-335f-885d-c3c12b7f5259",
                                                "text": "But to return to the Homily on St. Gregory. It is printed from a Tranſcript I had made of it from one made by Dr. Hopkins, I believe, out of the Cottonian Book, Vitellius D. 17. […] The Homily is one of thoſe which were prepared by Ælfrick, to be uſed in the Engliſh Saxon Church: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3db5be84-2ea8-4bc7-8825-3388f98d431d",
                                                "sense_id": "3c135975-e047-335f-885d-c3c12b7f5259",
                                                "text": "[W]e must pay attention not only to the rich tradition of the homily in the early Church and the retrieval of this preaching form by Vatican II but also to the evolving understandings of the homily from those who have tried to respond to the changing cultural patterns, pastoral needs, and theological trends of the day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d770176-2f4e-45e3-9086-9ed7c23dda1c",
                                                "sense_id": "3c135975-e047-335f-885d-c3c12b7f5259",
                                                "text": "[W]hen one approaches Origen's homilies, this aspect of the work of the priest must be kept in mind. The purpose of his sermons was to instruct and to lead beginners in the faith to a higher level of understanding and maturity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6550a0a-24ed-3567-865c-886e03bfdcf9",
                                        "entry_id": "1e35f580-cd44-39f8-8ad7-971fa504ac73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A moralizing lecture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43501e93-9d04-4dcd-b058-bade8ae619bd",
                                                "sense_id": "f6550a0a-24ed-3567-865c-886e03bfdcf9",
                                                "text": "How expreſſe and poſitive the doctrine of our Church is againſt them, our English Homily entitled Againſt the perill of idolatry, abundantly declareth; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99b28e4a-0ac6-4d5d-b557-2beaa599bf36",
                                                "sense_id": "f6550a0a-24ed-3567-865c-886e03bfdcf9",
                                                "text": "But if it be as I have heard my father / Deal out in his long homilies, 'tis a thing— / Oh God! I dare no think on 't!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "547c8b70-0230-4b81-9388-f8ab8ee27b44",
                                                "sense_id": "f6550a0a-24ed-3567-865c-886e03bfdcf9",
                                                "text": "Will it be said, that Literature and Christianity, are two distinct things? Or, that it would be preposterous to expect that every writer should give us a homily, when we want to laugh, or a sermon, when we wish to think?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2730d726-6d97-3ae6-bd13-4545b6d04275",
                                        "entry_id": "1e35f580-cd44-39f8-8ad7-971fa504ac73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A platitude."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "homily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5681bda-a1be-3cc3-a6e0-79797e78c5b4",
                                        "entry_id": "1c1aba51-4a97-31b5-acac-f61e1d7ef4b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a homey manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b83dac9b-0f25-49f0-9340-073293b9fe29",
                                                "sense_id": "b5681bda-a1be-3cc3-a6e0-79797e78c5b4",
                                                "text": "Rocky handed it [the beer] to Bob, whose demurrals petered out as he held the can's cold actuality in his hand. It bore the smiling face of Lynn Swann. He opened it. Leo farted homily to close the transaction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffb603f6-a06f-402e-80b6-17c0a9c397ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "9222bbfa-f6bc-3244-a253-0029e0eba6e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "0c66d921-2c89-35b0-b4bc-e8efbcdf9382",
                        "source_sense_description": "Christentum: eine Predigt in enger Anlehnung an einen Bibeltext, eine erbauliche Predigt",
                        "target_lang_word": "homélie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "homélie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f096077a-3c28-3a70-b891-a03b6d99ae78",
                                        "entry_id": "30c26532-14c1-3fdf-af7c-c198bbe911d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Discours expliquant les matières de la religion, et principalement l’évangile, en particulier après la lecture de l’évangile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eaadd0c1-d29d-49d7-afa0-211afe97e9fd",
                                                "sense_id": "f096077a-3c28-3a70-b891-a03b6d99ae78",
                                                "text": "La prédication se faisait tantôt en latin pour les clercs, tantôt en français pour le peuple. C’est dans l’homélie, le sermon, que la langue vulgaire a été employée d’abord, et cet emploi remonte jusqu’au IXᵉ siècle ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb3dd0ea-e77a-4264-a413-0e5e8f23953f",
                                                "sense_id": "f096077a-3c28-3a70-b891-a03b6d99ae78",
                                                "text": "J’ai composé sur son dos plus d’une homélie pour l’édification de mes frères du couvent et de beaucoup de pauvres âmes chrétiennes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91151616-eaac-49ba-ae7e-fb15a33ae18b",
                                                "sense_id": "f096077a-3c28-3a70-b891-a03b6d99ae78",
                                                "text": "Juste-Agénor de Baraglioul buvait une tasse de tisane en écoutant une homélie du père Avril, son confesseur, qu’il avait pris l’habitude de consulter fréquemment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "517512c0-9a26-3b64-94d2-9b38ed0f61a9",
                                        "entry_id": "30c26532-14c1-3fdf-af7c-c198bbe911d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Certaines leçons du bréviaire qui sont des extraits des homélies des pères, et qu’on chante au troisième nocturne des matines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff5cd08c-be53-3359-8bf6-ef3583e0dcf5",
                                        "entry_id": "30c26532-14c1-3fdf-af7c-c198bbe911d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ouvrage d’esprit, discours où se montre l’affectation de moraliser et qui cause de l’ennui."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcf8ac48-a8ed-4ce0-9580-aa018ee40e3c",
                                                "sense_id": "ff5cd08c-be53-3359-8bf6-ef3583e0dcf5",
                                                "text": "Aujourd’hui les homélies misérables d’un vieillard cauteleux, ennemi de la République, […], ont servi de texte à de nouvelles inculpations ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "699cdbaf-6c90-4bcf-ba46-f080194bfaac",
                                                "sense_id": "ff5cd08c-be53-3359-8bf6-ef3583e0dcf5",
                                                "text": "Trois ans, en chiffres ronds, passés à l’armée, n’avaient pas fait de Monsieur de C. un patriote prêt à donner des fils pour la reconquête de l’Alsace-Lorraine : il laissait ces grands élans à son cousin P., député de la droite, qui remplissait la Chambre de ses homélies en l’honneur de la natalité française."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "773203fb-e9a8-4148-a2ed-de7cbc66a630",
                                                "sense_id": "ff5cd08c-be53-3359-8bf6-ef3583e0dcf5",
                                                "text": "Après une intervention de Jacques Attali sur sa définition des “résignés réclamants”, au cours de laquelle il s’en prend implicitement à la vision du monde de son contradicteur, Eric Zemmour se lance dans un réquisitoire très incisif : J’ai écouté l’homélie du père Attali et je suis encore un peu ébloui. […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
